  "response": "**Solution**\n\nCount numbers from 1–1000 divisible by 3 or 5, then remove those also divisible by 7.\n\nStep 1: Divisible by 3 or 5 (inclusion-exclusion):\n- ⌊1000/3⌋ = 333\n- ⌊1000/5⌋ = 200\n- ⌊1000/15⌋ = 66\n- Total = 333 + 200 − 66 = 467\n\nStep 2: Among these, subtract those also divisible by 7 (i.e., divisible by 21 or 35):\n- ⌊1000/21⌋ = 47\n- ⌊1000/35⌋ = 28\n- ⌊1000/105⌋ = 9\n- Total = 47 + 28 − 9 = 66\n\nStep 3: Final count = 467 − 66 = 401\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 401",
